==Diseases==
''E. minor'' is the only known [[host (epidemiology)|host]] {{As of|2023|lc=yes}} of the {{Vanchor|Eragrostis minor streak virus|text=''Eragrostis minor'' streak virus}}.<ref name="Find and sequence new ornamental grass virus">{{Cite journal|year=2011|volume=156|pages=1299–1303|department=Annotated Sequence Record|s2cid=3151261|pmid=21614438|doi=10.1007/s00705-011-1026-8|first1=Darren P.|last1=Martin|first2=Daphne|last2=Linderme|first3=Pierre|last3=Lefeuvre|first4=Dionne N.|last4=Shepherd|first5=Arvind|last5=Varsani|title=''Eragrostis minor'' streak virus: an Asian streak virus in Africa|journal=Archives of Virology |issue=7 }} Cited by Karavina ''et al.'', 2014.</ref>

